{
 "$comment": [
  "The LPS 3D object catalogue: `display3d(F, [type:model, model:tree, \u2026])`.",
  "",
  "These are BUILT, not downloaded \u2014 each is a handful of three.js primitives",
  "in ui/src/models3d.js (a tree is a cylinder and two cones; a truck is a",
  "cab, a bed and four wheels). The CC0 mesh libraries were looked at first",
  "and are the right answer for a game: Kenney (https://kenney.nl/assets),",
  "Quaternius (https://quaternius.com) and Poly Pizza (https://poly.pizza)",
  "all ship glTF under CC0. What they cost here is megabytes in the",
  "repository, a loader in the bundle, and a fetch at build time \u2014 for",
  "objects that a scene shows at the size of a thumb, in a picture whose",
  "point is which fluent holds. A primitive composition costs none of that,",
  "takes the object's own colour, and cannot rot. The door is left open: a",
  "model name could later resolve to a mesh instead.",
  "",
  "`concepts` is what the assistant matches on, as for the icons and the",
  "patterns: the words a thing in a program is likely to be called."
 ],
